Package: omnipath.client
Type: Package
Title: Query OmniPath through Its API or Locally with DuckDB
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jonathan", "Schaul", email = "schauljonathan@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: The explorer's search, relation export and entity details, answered by
    the hosted OmniPath API (the default) or from a local installation: versioned
    OmniPath resources (Parquet files) downloaded into a data directory and written
    into the DuckDB database the API serves a release from, which also takes any
    SQL. Both modes give the same answers as the Python client 'omnipath_client'.
    Both clients read and write the same data directory.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    DBI,
    duckdb (>= 1.5.0),
    httr2 (>= 1.0.0),
    jsonlite
Suggests:
    dbplyr,
    dplyr,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
